Docs - what this desktop can do
===============================

This directory has a guide to each of the things this desktop adds to
RISC OS 3.71. Double-click one to read it (it opens in Edit).

  Browse        !Browse, a web browser for today's web: in Apps
  GameLib       !GameLib, the library of game parts (main loop,
                drawing, keys, sound, scores) that games import: in
                !Boot.Resources
  GraphTask     !GraphTask, which runs BBC BASIC programs in windows
                on the desktop, graphics and all: in Apps
  HostFS        using folders from the computer running your web
                browser as RISC OS discs, with !HostFS in Utilities
  JsEdit        !JsEdit, the programmer's editor for JavaScript,
                BASIC and Obey: in Apps
  Journal       !Journal, a diary with a page for every day, a
                calendar, Find and a password lock: in Apps
  Lander2       Lander II, a Zarch-like game grown from Braben's
                Lander, whose JavaScript you can read and change:
                in Diversions
  Letters       !Letters, which reads Microsoft Word (.docx) files, lets
                you select, type, delete and undo, copy, cut and
                paste (within !Letters and with other programs), find
                and replace, format text (keys, Format menu,
                toolbar, ruler), set line spacing, the space around
                paragraphs and flow options (the Paragraph box),
                set tab stops (the ruler, the Tabs box), put lines
                round paragraphs and shade them or their text
                (Format > Borders and shading), change case (Format
                > Change case, SHIFT-F3), copy the look of text
                (the format painter), zoom the page, shows and
                edits bulleted and numbered lists (Tab, SHIFT-Tab,
                Backspace), makes new lists (the Bullets and
                Numbering buttons, CTRL-SHIFT-L, typing * or 1. and
                a space), puts in page and section breaks, symbols
                and special characters (the Insert menu, CTRL-Enter,
                the Symbol window), hyperlinks (CTRL-K) and
                bookmarks (CTRL-SHIFT-F5), shows pictures and lets
                you resize, delete, describe, put in (Insert >
                Picture...), drop, paste and copy them (the Picture
                box), shows tables (lines, shading, merged cells and
                table styles), lets you type, select and format
                in their cells, and makes tables and changes their
                rows, columns and cells (Insert > Table..., the
                Table menu), sets their width, alignment, row
                heights, lines and shading (Table properties...,
                Cell alignment, Borders and shading...), lets
                you drag the edges of columns and rows, copies and
                pastes cells, rows and tables (also to and from
                other programs), converts text to a table and a
                table to text (Table > Convert), counts words
                (Edit > Word count), shows documents as pages
                (Print layout on the View menu; pages broken by
                Word's rules, tables split across pages), as one
                long page (Draft), as wide as the window (Web
                layout) or as an outline of its headings to fold,
                promote, demote and move (Outline), sets up the
                paper, margins and section
                starts (Format > Page setup, Layout), puts in
                even and odd page section breaks, shows headers
                and footers and edits them (double-click one, the
                Header menu), shows page numbers, dates and other
                fields worked out for each page (Insert > Page
                number, Field..., Edit > Update field, View >
                Field codes), sets text in newspaper columns
                (Format > Columns..., Insert > Column break),
                numbers lines (Format > Layout... > Line
                numbers...), places floating pictures and
                tables on their pages with text flowing round
                them (Format > Wrap text), applies, makes,
                changes and deletes styles (the Style list,
                CTRL-SHIFT-S, Format > Styles...), shows footnotes
                and endnotes (on the pages, in Print layout), puts
                them in (Insert > Footnote, CTRL-ALT-F; Endnote,
                CTRL-ALT-D), lets you write them in the note mode,
                numbers them, converts them and counts their words,
                makes and updates tables of contents and of
                figures (Insert > Table of Contents..., Table of
                Figures...), captions (Insert > Caption...) and
                cross-references (Insert > Cross-reference...),
                updates fields (Edit > Update field, Update all
                fields), makes new documents, lists recent files,
                and saves documents (Save, Save as, Save a copy,
                Revert;
                closing, quitting and shutting down ask first)
                losing nothing: in MoreApps
  Memory        the computer's memory: how much RAM it has (4MB to
                256MB, chosen in !Configure) and the Task Manager's
                figures and bars
  Pacman        !Pacman, a tribute to the 1980 arcade maze game, whose
                JavaScript you can read and change: in Diversions
  Programming   writing your own programs in JavaScript: the two
                books in Manuals, and their examples
  Server        using the desktop from another computer, with a
                shared Server drive and a browser on the server

Elsewhere on the hard disc:

  Apps          the applications (!Draw, !Paint and the rest are also
                on the Apps icon on the icon bar)
  Manuals       the RISC OS User Guide and the programming books, read
                with !Bookworm (double-click a file ending /htm)
  MoreApps      !Letters, the word processor for Word files
  !Boot         the boot sequence and the system resources; in
                !Boot.Resources are !WimpLib, the library of shared
                JavaScript modules that programs on the disc import
                (see Letters, part 21), and !GameLib, the library for
                games (see GameLib)
  Examples      example programs, including those from the books
  Demos, Diversions, Tutorials   things to try (Demos.BASIC has BASIC
                programs: drag them to !GraphTask to run them in
                windows)
  Utilities     tools, such as !HostFS

Press F12 for the command line; *Help lists its commands.
